# 🔍 Frontend QA Report — SmartLearn LMS (Learning-Hub)

**Project:** SmartLearn LMS  
**Stack:** Next.js 15 · React 19 · TailwindCSS v4 · Radix UI · TanStack Query · NextAuth · Prisma  
**Report Date:** 2026-02-26  
**Reviewer:** Antigravity AI  

---

## Executive Summary

The frontend is a well-structured Next.js 15 application with a solid design system, role-based routing, dark-mode support, and performance optimizations already in place (lazy loading, memoization, `next/font`, image optimization). However, several issues across **code quality, security, accessibility, and maintainability** require attention before a production release.

| Severity | Count |
|---|---|
| 🔴 Critical | 3 |
| 🟠 High | 5 |
| 🟡 Medium | 7 |
| 🟢 Low / Enhancement | 6 |
| **Total** | **21** |

---

## 1. Code Quality & Build Configuration

### 🔴 CRITICAL — ESLint and TypeScript Errors Silenced in Builds
**File:** [next.config.mjs](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/next.config.mjs) (lines 3–8)

```js
eslint: { ignoreDuringBuilds: true },
typescript: { ignoreBuildErrors: true },
```

This suppresses all linting and type errors during `next build`. Real bugs (type mismatches, unused variables, dead code) can silently ship to production.

**Fix:** Remove both flags. Address all ESLint and TypeScript errors, then re-enable enforcement.

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Production `console.log` Statements
**Files affected:** [video-player.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/video-player.js), [app/instructor/courses/create/page.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/instructor/courses/create/page.js), `app/student/browse-course/[id]/enroll-manual/page.jsx`, and many API routes.

Debug logs with messages like `[v0] Fetching video token`, `[v0] 🎉 Video completed!`, progress percentages etc. are left in production code. These:
- Expose internal logic and API paths to browser DevTools
- Create noise in server logs
- May expose user data (user ID, video ID, course ID)

**Fix:** Replace with a conditional logger (`if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development')`) or use a logging library. Remove all `[v0]`-prefixed debug logs.

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Massive Duplicate Code in Sidebars
**Files:** [student-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/student-sidebar.jsx) (518 lines) and [instructor-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/instructor-sidebar.jsx) (522 lines)

Both sidebars share ~85% identical JSX: mobile menu bar, desktop collapsible sidebar, user section, logout button, badge logic, and localStorage polling. The logic is copy-pasted and diverges in minor ways (role checks, menu items), making bugs harder to fix and features harder to add.

**Fix:** Extract a shared `<AppSidebar menuItems={...} badgeConfig={...} portalLabel={...} />` component, reducing each file to ~80 lines of configuration.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — `allMenuItems` Array Recreated on Every Render
**File:** [instructor-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/instructor-sidebar.jsx) (lines 36–63)

`allMenuItems` is declared as a plain array inside the component body, so it is recreated on every render.  The `menuItems` `useMemo` filters it, but `allMenuItems` itself is not memoized.

**Fix:** Move `allMenuItems` outside the component or wrap it in `useMemo`.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — [isActive](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/instructor-sidebar.jsx#80-81) Not Memoized in Instructor Sidebar
**File:** [instructor-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/instructor-sidebar.jsx) (line 80)

```js
const isActive = (href) => pathname === href
```

Unlike [student-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/student-sidebar.jsx) which uses `useCallback`, the instructor sidebar recreates this function every render.

**Fix:** Wrap with `useCallback(() => ..., [pathname])`.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — [fetch](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/video-player.js#125-166) Error in [video-player.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/video-player.js) Dependency Array Bug
**File:** [video-player.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/video-player.js) (line 174)

```js
}, [videoId, courseId, error])
```

The `error` state is included in the deps of the token-fetch effect. If token fetching fails and sets `error`, the effect re-runs, potentially triggering an infinite fetch loop.

**Fix:** Remove `error` from the dependency array. Use a `hasFetched` ref to guard the effect.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — `localStorage` Polling Every 500ms
**Files:** [student-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/student-sidebar.jsx) (lines 165, 201), [instructor-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/instructor-sidebar.jsx) (lines 195, 231)

A `setInterval(checkViewed, 500)` is running continuously per sidebar mount to work around the fact that `storage` events don't fire within the same tab. This is inefficient.

**Fix:** Use a Zustand store (already in the project) or React Context to share the `viewed` flag in-process, eliminating the polling entirely.

---

### 🟢 LOW — Commented-Out Menu Items
**Files:** [student-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/student-sidebar.jsx) (lines 48–49), [instructor-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/instructor-sidebar.jsx) (lines 52–55)

Wishlist, Notifications, Earnings, Analytics, and Messages are commented out. This indicates unfinished features left in code.

**Fix:** Move to a feature-flag pattern or a separate `upcomingMenuItems` array with a clear label.

