## 2. Security

### 🔴 CRITICAL — `'unsafe-inline'` and `'unsafe-eval'` in CSP
**File:** [next.config.mjs](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/next.config.mjs) (lines 81–82)

```
script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval' 'unsafe-inline' https://embed.cloudflarestream.com
style-src  'self' 'unsafe-inline'
```

`unsafe-eval` enables `eval()` and the Function constructor — a common XSS exploitation path. `unsafe-inline` allows inline scripts and styles, weakening CSP protection. React itself does not need `unsafe-eval` in production builds.

**Fix:** Use nonce-based CSP (`'nonce-xxx'`) with Next.js middleware for inline scripts, and remove `unsafe-eval`. Tailwind v4 also supports hashed inline styles.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — "Forgot Password" Button Has No Implementation
**File:** [app/auth/signin/page.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/auth/signin/page.js) (lines 166–171)

```jsx
<button type="button" className="...">
  Forgot?
</button>
```

The button is present and clickable but does nothing — no `onClick` handler, no route, no API. Users who forget their password are silently stuck.

**Fix:** Implement a password reset flow (email + token) or remove the button and add it back when the feature is ready.

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Open Redirect Risk on Sign-In `callbackUrl`
**File:** [app/auth/signin/page.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/auth/signin/page.js) (line 20)

```js
const callbackUrl = useMemo(() => searchParams.get("callbackUrl") || "/student", [searchParams])
```

`callbackUrl` is read directly from URL params without validation. An attacker can craft `?callbackUrl=https://evil.com` and redirect a user there after login.

**Fix:**
```js
const rawUrl = searchParams.get("callbackUrl") || "/student"
const callbackUrl = rawUrl.startsWith("/") ? rawUrl : "/student"
```

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — `dangerouslyAllowSVG: true` Without Restricted CSP
**File:** [next.config.mjs](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/next.config.mjs) (line 16)

SVG files can contain embedded JavaScript. The `contentSecurityPolicy` for SVGs is set to `sandbox` which is correct, but given the relaxed global CSP (`unsafe-inline`) this protection layer is weakened.

**Fix:** Keep `dangerouslyAllowSVG: true` only if user-uploaded SVGs are served; otherwise remove it.

---

## 3. Accessibility (a11y)

### 🟠 HIGH — Raw `<img>` Tags Used Instead of `next/image`
**File:** [app/student/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/student/page.jsx) (lines 153–157)

```jsx
<img
  src={enrollment.course.thumbnail || "/placeholder.svg"}
  alt={enrollment.course.title}
  className="w-full h-32 sm:h-40 object-cover"
/>
```

Raw `<img>` tags bypass Next.js image optimization (lazy loading, WebP conversion, size hints). The same pattern exists in [app/dashboard/page.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/dashboard/page.js), [wishlist/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/student/wishlist/page.jsx), and [instructor/enrollments/pending/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/instructor/enrollments/pending/page.jsx).

**Fix:** Replace with `<Image src={...} alt={...} fill className="object-cover" />` using Next.js [Image](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/Home/HeroSection.jsx#71-172) component wrapped in a `relative` container.

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Mobile Menu Toggle Button Has No `aria-label` on Instructor Sidebar
**File:** [instructor-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/instructor-sidebar.jsx) (lines 271–275)

```jsx
<button onClick={() => setMobileMenuOpen(!mobileMenuOpen)} className="...">
  {mobileMenuOpen ? <X /> : <Menu />}
</button>
```

The button has no `aria-label`. Screen readers will announce it as an unlabeled button.

**Fix:** Add `aria-label={mobileMenuOpen ? "Close menu" : "Open menu"}` and `aria-expanded={mobileMenuOpen}`.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — `<label>` Elements Not Linked to Inputs
**File:** [app/auth/signin/page.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/auth/signin/page.js) (lines 147, 165)

```jsx
<label className="...">Email Address</label>
<input type="email" ... />
```

The `<label>` has no `htmlFor` attribute, and the `<input>` has no [id](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/providers.js#9-35). They are not programmatically associated.

**Fix:** Add `htmlFor="email"` to the label and `id="email"` to the input. Same fix needed for the password field.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Aria Label Mismatch in HeroSection Stats
**File:** [components/Home/HeroSection.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/Home/HeroSection.jsx) (line 314)

The `aria-label="50,000 plus students"` says "50,000" but the visible text reads "10K+". Screen reader users get different information than sighted users.

**Fix:** Align `aria-label` with actual displayed value: `aria-label="10,000 plus students"`.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Video Player Has No Accessible Controls or Skip Option
**File:** [components/video-player.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/video-player.js)

The video player is implemented as a raw `<iframe>` injection with no surrounding accessible wrapper (`role="region"`, `aria-label="Video player"`). Keyboard-only and screen-reader users cannot navigate to or around the player easily.

**Fix:** Add `role="region"` and `aria-label="Course video player"` to the outer container div.

---

## 4. Performance

### 🟡 MEDIUM — `style jsx` Inline CSS in HeroSection
**File:** [components/Home/HeroSection.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/Home/HeroSection.jsx) (lines 371–381)

```jsx
<style jsx>{`
  @keyframes float { ... }
`}</style>
```

`styled-jsx` is a Next.js Pages Router feature, not App Router. In the App Router context this may work but adds an unnecessary runtime dependency and injects a non-cacheable `<style>` tag on every render.

**Fix:** Move the `@keyframes float` animation to [globals.css](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/globals.css).

---

### 🟢 LOW — Redundant CSS: Both `@layer base` and Regular Rules Apply Same Styles
**File:** [app/globals.css](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/globals.css) (lines 261–278)

```css
@layer base { body { @apply bg-background text-foreground; } }
/* Then immediately after: */
body { background-color: var(--background); color: var(--foreground); }
```

The same styles are defined twice — once inside `@layer base` and once as a regular rule.

**Fix:** Remove the duplicate regular rules at lines 274–279 and keep only the `@layer base` version.

---

### 🟢 LOW — Inline `style` Attribute for Background Gradient Duplication in HeroSection
**File:** [components/Home/HeroSection.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/Home/HeroSection.jsx) (lines 194–197)

Both a Tailwind `bg-gradient-to-br` class and an inline `style={{ background: ... }}` are applied to the same `<section>`. The inline style wins and the Tailwind class is redundant.

**Fix:** Remove the Tailwind gradient class and keep only the inline style (or vice versa — define a CSS variable-based Tailwind utility).

---

## 5. UX Issues

### 🟠 HIGH — Error State Silently Falls Through on Student Dashboard
**File:** [app/student/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/student/page.jsx) (lines 53–56)

```jsx
if (isError) {
  console.error("Error fetching enrollments:", error)
  // Still render the page with empty data, but could show error message
}
```

When the API fails, the user sees an empty dashboard with no feedback (no toast, no error banner). The developer comment even acknowledges this is incomplete.

**Fix:** Show a user-visible error state — a toast notification or an inline alert card: *"We couldn't load your courses. Please refresh."*

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — `placeholder.svg` Used as Fallback but File May Not Exist
**Files:** [app/student/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/student/page.jsx), [app/dashboard/page.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/dashboard/page.js), [app/student/wishlist/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/student/wishlist/page.jsx), [app/instructor/enrollments/pending/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/instructor/enrollments/pending/page.jsx), [components/image-upload.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/image-upload.jsx)

`"/placeholder.svg"` is referenced as a fallback but there is no `placeholder.svg` in the `public/` directory (only `public/images/` subdirectory was found).

**Fix:** Either create `public/placeholder.svg` or replace with a Tailwind-based skeleton/gradient placeholder div.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Student Dashboard Shows Only 3 Recent Courses (Hardcoded Slice)
**File:** [app/student/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/student/page.jsx) (line 44)

```js
const enrolledCourses = enrollmentData?.enrollments?.slice(0, 3) || []
```

The limit is hardcoded. If a student has 10+ courses, they see only 3 with no pagination or "show more" option (the "View All" link exists but only in proximity, not clearly tied to this limit).

**Fix:** Either increase the limit or add a visible "Showing 3 of N" label so the experience is predictable.

---

### 🟢 LOW — "Active Learner" / "Expert Educator" Labels Are Hardcoded
**Files:** [student-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/student-sidebar.jsx) (line 338), [instructor-sidebar.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/instructor-sidebar.jsx) (line 344)

All students display "Active Learner" and all instructors display "Expert Educator" regardless of their actual activity status.

**Fix:** Derive this from real data (completion rate, enrollment count) or remove it entirely to avoid misleading users.

---

### 🟢 LOW — Watermark Uses `Math.random()` Directly in Render
**File:** [components/video-player.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/components/video-player.js) (lines 81–89)

The `Math.random()` call in the watermark interval effect contains a randomized interval duration (`Math.random() * 5000 + 5000`) which is fine, but the initial interval fires immediately on mount without a random offset. This means all video players on the same session start their watermark cycle in sync.

**Fix:** Vary the initial delay with a small random offset on mount.

---

## 6. Architecture & Patterns

| Issue | File | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|
| Sidebar state (`sidebarOpen`) in a Zustand `useDashboard` store is good — but delivery/session "viewed" state also belongs in that store | Both sidebars | Move `hasViewedDeliveries`, `hasViewedLiveSessions`, etc. to Zustand to eliminate localStorage polling |
| [app/dashboard/page.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/dashboard/page.js) appears to be a duplicate of [app/student/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/student/page.jsx) | `app/dashboard/` | Verify if this route is still used; if not, delete it |
| Metadata `generator: "v0.app"` leaks AI tool attribution | [app/layout.js](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/layout.js) line 34 | Remove or change to your own tool identifier |
| No loading skeleton; `LoadingBubbles` replaces the entire page layout | [app/student/page.jsx](file:///Users/naveen/Manusha/Learning-Hub/app/student/page.jsx) | Use skeleton cards that match the layout for better perceived performance |
| No test files found anywhere in the codebase | Entire project | Add unit tests (Vitest/Jest) for utility functions and Integration tests (Playwright) for auth flows |

